['A team changes document normalization but keeps old vectors. What should it assess?','Vector-space compatibility','Only the welcome screen','Only output font size','Only the model nickname','Material preprocessing changes can alter what the index represents and how queries should match.','Screens do not define vectors.','Fonts do not repair representation drift.','Names are not sufficient version metadata.'],
['A model is accurate but violates a hard data-location requirement. What follows?','It may be ineligible','Quality overrides every policy','A renamed setting fixes privacy','Only the average score matters','Operational/privacy constraints must be satisfied alongside retrieval quality.','Performance does not grant data rights.','Renaming does not change deployment.','Averages do not establish compliance.']
