{slug:'precision',comp:'m3.c1',title:'Measure precision at k with explicit relevance judgments',before:'Understand ranked candidates and query-specific relevance labels. Distinguish similarity scores from judged usefulness.',intro:'A university search returns five policy passages. If only two answer the question, a high-looking similarity score should not hide the irrelevant material shown to students.',sections:[S('Define the denominator and labeling policy','Precision at k measures how many of the top k retrieved items are relevant, divided by the declared k under the evaluation convention. Document how short result lists, ties and duplicate chunks are handled. A relevance judgment must specify whether the unit is a chunk, parent document or answer-supporting passage.','Labels can be graded or binary, but the metric and scorer must match the declared definition. A passage about the same topic may not count as relevant if the task requires a specific exception or date. Keep the judgment policy reviewable.'),S('Interpret the metric within the product','High precision means less irrelevant material among returned candidates; it does not imply all relevant sources were found. Increasing k can expose more useful passages while also adding noise and cost. Evaluate at the k the product can actually consume.','The fixture uses a fixed top-four list and binary synthetic labels. It does not establish real relevance, label quality or a production ranking benchmark.')],problem:'Calculate precision at four for a synthetic judged result list.',code:'ranking = ["p1", "p2", "p3", "p4", "p5"]\nrelevant = {"p1", "p3", "p6"}\nk = 4\nhits = sum(doc in relevant for doc in ranking[:k])\nprint(hits)\nprint(f"{hits / k:.2f}")\nprint(ranking[:k])',expect:"2\n0.50\n['p1', 'p2', 'p3', 'p4']",steps:['Choose the declared evaluation cutoff.','Count judged relevant items within that prefix.','Divide by the declared k and retain the inspected result ids.'],limit:'The relevance set is invented and complete only by assumption. This computes one query’s metric, not representative search quality or agreement among real reviewers.',mistakes:['Using a similarity threshold as if it were a human relevance label.','Changing the denominator silently for different result lengths.'],takeaways:['Define relevance units and denominator conventions.','Evaluate at the product’s usable cutoff.'],refs:['embedding-search','embedding-qa'],questions:[
['What does precision at k emphasize?','Top-k relevant share','All relevant sources found','The model’s training loss','Current provider spending','Precision describes how much of the inspected result prefix is judged relevant.','That is closer to recall’s purpose.','Training loss is a different measure.','Cost needs separate accounting.'],
['What is required before computing a meaningful precision score?','A relevance judgment policy','Only cosine values','Only document titles','Only a larger result count','The metric needs a definition of relevance and the unit being judged.','Similarity is not a ground-truth label.','Titles can be insufficient.','Count does not define usefulness.'],
['Two relevant hits among four inspected results give what precision?','0.50','0.25','2.00','1.00','Under the declared full-k convention, precision is 2 divided by 4.','That would count one hit.','Precision is a fraction here.','Not all results are relevant.'],
['A result list has fewer than k items. What should evaluation document?','The denominator rule','Only the UI card size','Only the model logo','Only query punctuation','Short lists need an explicit consistent metric policy so scores remain interpretable.','Layout does not define the formula.','Branding is unrelated.','Punctuation does not choose a denominator.'],
['Three top results are overlapping chunks of one passage. What labeling issue needs review?','Judged evidence units','Only token spelling','Only the document font','Only the index nickname','Chunk-level versus document-level evaluation can differ when duplicate evidence fills the prefix.','Spelling is not the unit definition.','Fonts do not deduplicate evidence.','Names do not establish metric semantics.'],
['Precision improves at k=2 but the app consumes ten results. What should be checked?','Quality at the actual cutoff','Only the best-looking number','Only the first result title','Only a wider viewport','The metric should match the product’s retrieval/context budget and usage.','Selective reporting can hide noise.','One title does not characterize ten results.','Screen width does not define relevance.'],
['A top passage discusses fees but not the requested exception. What should the rubric decide?','Whether it supports the task','Only if it has many keywords','Only if its score is high','Only if it is long','Relevance should follow the actual information need rather than superficial topic overlap.','Keywords can be misleading.','A score is not a label.','Length does not prove support.'],
['A fixture computes precision from invented labels. What remains unproved?','Real judgment quality','The numerator arithmetic','The ranking prefix ids','The local decimal display','Synthetic arithmetic does not establish whether actual reviewers would label documents correctly.','The count is executed.','The prefix is explicit.','Formatting is locally observed.']
]},
{slug:'recall',comp:'m3.c1',title:'Measure recall at k and distinguish missing evidence from noise',before:'Use precision-at-k definitions and a declared relevance unit. Recall needs an appropriate relevant-item denominator.',intro:'A logistics search returns two excellent passages but misses the one containing an important delivery exception. Precision alone cannot reveal that omission.',sections:[S('Recall asks what relevant material was missed','Recall at k divides the number of retrieved relevant items in the top k by the total relevant items under the evaluation set’s judgment policy. The denominator needs care: real corpora often have incomplete judgments, and unjudged does not automatically mean irrelevant.','Define behavior for queries with no known relevant items rather than dividing by zero or inventing a perfect score. Report such cases separately when they represent the product’s no-answer behavior. Keep precision and recall distinct so high relevance among returned results does not hide missing evidence.'),S('Tune candidate budgets with downstream constraints','Increasing k can improve recall but also adds irrelevant material, latency and generation-context cost. A reranker may improve order among candidates but cannot recover a passage never retrieved into its candidate set. Evaluate the entire pipeline at explicit cutoffs.','The fixture computes precision and recall for the same synthetic ranking. It shows that their denominators differ and does not claim exhaustive real-world relevance judgments.')],problem:'Compare precision and recall for the same synthetic top-three results.',code:'ranking = ["a", "b", "c", "d"]\nrelevant = {"a", "c", "e", "f"}\nk = 3\nhits = len(set(ranking[:k]) & relevant)\nprint(f"precision={hits / k:.3f}")\nprint(f"recall={hits / len(relevant):.3f}")\nprint(sorted(relevant - set(ranking[:k])))',expect:"precision=0.667\nrecall=0.500\n['e', 'f']",steps:['Use one declared relevance set and top-k prefix.','Compute precision and recall with different denominators.','Inspect which known relevant items were missed.'],limit:'The fixture assumes complete binary judgments over unique ids. It does not estimate unknown relevant documents, prove real annotation completeness or measure live retrieval latency.',mistakes:['Calling high precision proof that no relevant source was missed.','Treating unjudged documents as definitively irrelevant without a policy.'],takeaways:['Recall depends on the relevant-item denominator.','Inspect missing evidence and no-answer queries explicitly.'],refs:['embedding-search','embedding-qa'],questions:[
['What is recall at k’s denominator under complete binary judgments?','Total relevant items','All returned items only','The vector dimension','The number of user accounts','Recall measures the retrieved share of the known relevant set.','That denominator fits precision-like calculations.','Dimension is not relevance count.','Accounts do not define this metric.'],
['Can high precision coexist with low recall?','Yes, useful items can be missed','No, the metrics are identical','No, high scores find everything','No, when k is numeric','A small clean result set can omit many relevant sources.','The denominators differ.','Ranking scores do not guarantee coverage.','The cutoff does not make the metrics equal.'],
['What requires an explicit policy when there are no known relevant items?','Recall’s zero denominator','The existence of strings','The browser color palette','The model’s display name','An empty relevant set needs a defined no-answer/evaluation treatment rather than unchecked division.','String existence is unrelated.','Colors do not define the metric.','Names do not resolve zero division.'],
['A search returns two relevant items out of four known relevant items. What is recall under the stated convention?','0.50','0.25','2.00','1.00','The known retrieved share is two divided by four.','That would represent one of four.','The fraction cannot be two here.','Half the relevant items are missed.'],
['A reranker sees only the initial top twenty candidates. What can it not recover by reordering alone?','An absent relevant passage','A new order among candidates','A higher-ranked existing item','A tie-break among supplied ids','Reranking cannot select evidence that was never included in its candidate set.','Reordering supplied candidates is its role.','An existing candidate can move upward.','Ties can be resolved within the set.'],
['The corpus labels are incomplete. How should unjudged results be interpreted?','Under a documented judgment policy','Automatically irrelevant forever','Automatically relevant always','As proof of model truth','Incomplete judgments limit metric interpretation and need explicit treatment.','Missing labels are not definitive negative evidence.','Missing labels are not positive evidence either.','Judgment gaps do not prove facts.'],
['Increasing k finds more relevant sources but adds noise. What should tuning compare?','Recall, precision and cost','Only recall in isolation','Only the longest document','Only the UI button label','The retrieval budget has usefulness and resource tradeoffs that need joint evaluation.','One metric can hide downstream harm.','Length is not the tradeoff objective.','Labels do not measure quality.'],
['The fixture lists missed ids e and f. What does that establish?','Misses under supplied judgments','All real sources are known','A live index was queried','The model cannot answer any query','The set difference identifies omissions relative to the synthetic relevance set.','Completeness is assumed, not established.','No index call occurs.','One toy query does not imply universal failure.']
]},
{slug:'evaluation-cases',comp:'m3.c1',title:'Build a retrieval evaluation that survives model and chunk changes',before:'Use precision, recall, relevance-unit and no-answer definitions. Review fixed-case evaluation principles.',intro:'A retailer changes its chunker and embedding model. A useful evaluation must reveal whether query types improve or regress without mistaking new chunk identifiers for lost source evidence.',sections:[S('Version the whole retrieval experiment','Record document snapshot, chunking settings, embedding model/version, metric, filters, index configuration, query set and relevance judgments. A score without these conditions is hard to reproduce or interpret after the corpus changes.','Keep train/development and held-out evaluation roles clear. Avoid fitting every threshold to the final test set. Include exact-code, paraphrase, multilingual, ambiguous and no-answer cases, plus access-boundary tests that must never return unauthorized material.'),S('Use stable source meaning across changing chunks','When chunk boundaries change, exact chunk ids may not represent the same evidence unit. Maintain source/version/location mapping and a rubric that can judge the required passage rather than blindly compare obsolete chunk ids. Aggregate results by meaningful query segment and inspect regressions.','The fixture computes a macro average from two synthetic per-query precision values. It shows equal query weighting rather than pooling all hits into one denominator. It does not prove statistical significance, representative sampling or production adequacy.')],problem:'Compare query-weighted and pooled precision under synthetic result counts.',code:'queries = [{"hits": 1, "k": 1}, {"hits": 1, "k": 4}]\nmacro = sum(q["hits"] / q["k"] for q in queries) / len(queries)\npooled = sum(q["hits"] for q in queries) / sum(q["k"] for q in queries)\nprint(f"macro={macro:.3f}")\nprint(f"pooled={pooled:.3f}")\nprint(macro != pooled)',expect:'macro=0.625\npooled=0.400\nTrue',steps:['Compute each query’s declared precision.','Average queries equally for the macro metric.','Contrast with pooled hit/count weighting.'],limit:'Two invented queries only demonstrate aggregation semantics. They are not a retrieval benchmark, confidence estimate or basis for a current model recommendation.',mistakes:['Comparing scores from different corpus snapshots as if only the model changed.','Hiding critical segment regressions behind one aggregate.'],takeaways:['Version the full experiment and preserve evidence mappings.','Report metric definitions and important segments explicitly.'],refs:['embedding-search','embedding-chunks','embedding-qa'],questions:[
['What must a reproducible retrieval report identify?','Experiment versions','Only the best score','Only the model’s logo','Only a screenshot of results','Model, corpus, chunking, metrics, queries and judgments all affect the result.','A number lacks its conditions.','Branding does not identify the experiment.','Screenshots omit key configuration.'],
['Why can changed chunk ids complicate comparison?','The evidence units changed','All source meaning disappeared','Cosine stopped using numbers','Every new id is irrelevant','New boundaries may represent the same source evidence under different units and locations.','Meaning can remain available.','The metric still has numeric semantics.','Ids alone do not define relevance.'],
['What does a macro average weight equally in the fixture?','Queries','All result positions pooled','Vector coordinates','Source publication years','The macro calculation averages per-query values rather than pooling every denominator.','Pooled precision uses a different weighting.','Coordinates are not the units averaged.','Years are unrelated.'],
['A new model raises the overall mean but hurts Urdu exact-code queries. What should the report include?','The segment regression','Only the improved mean','Only the prompt font','Only the index name','Important query segments can regress despite an aggregate gain.','The mean can conceal a required-language failure.','Fonts do not measure retrieval.','Names do not expose performance.'],
['A threshold is repeatedly tuned on final test answers. What evidence weakens?','Independent final evaluation','The existence of stored queries','The local score arithmetic','The ability to sort results','Using final answers to guide choices makes the set part of development rather than untouched holdout evidence.','Queries can still exist.','Arithmetic can remain correct.','Sorting is separate.'],
['The corpus changes and a relevant policy is deleted. What must metric interpretation consider?','The source snapshot and labels','Only model temperature','Only UI theme','Only query timestamp formatting','Judgments must match the corpus version to distinguish legitimate source changes from retrieval defects.','Sampling does not define corpus membership.','Themes do not update labels.','Formatting is not source applicability.'],
['A retrieval suite has no no-answer queries. What behavior is untested?','No-evidence outcomes','Only ranking positive cases','Only local vector arithmetic','Only result-card rendering','The product needs evidence for queries that should not yield a supported answer.','Positive cases can still be tested.','Arithmetic may have separate checks.','Rendering is a different concern.'],
['Macro precision differs from pooled precision in the fixture. What should reporting do?','Name the aggregation convention','Choose the larger number silently','Claim one metric is universally correct','Hide the query counts','Different weightings answer different questions and need explicit interpretation.','Selective reporting misleads.','Suitability depends on the evaluation goal.','Counts help explain the difference.']
]}
